{"name":"California","hex":"#e98c3a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"California","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The most populous state of the United States. Capital: Sacramento. Largest city: Los Angeles.","A region on the west coast of North America comprising the US state of California and the Baja California peninsula in Mexico; historically also including other areas in Alta California and Baja California."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/California"}],"entries":[{"title":"California","blocks":[{"text":"California is a state in the Western United States. It is bordered by Oregon to the north, the Mexican state of Baja California to the south, Nevada to the east, Arizona to the southeast, and the Pacific Ocean to the west. With a population of over 39 million across an area of 163,696 square miles (423,970 km2), it is the most populous U.S. state and the third largest by land area."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Flag_of_California.svg/330px-Flag_of_California.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/California","wikidata":"Q99"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/2005_CA_Proof.png/500px-2005_CA_Proof.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/2005_CA_Proof.png/500px-2005_CA_Proof.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2005_CA_Proof.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/California_tribes_%26_languages_at_contact.png/500px-California_tribes_%26_languages_at_contact.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/California_tribes_%26_languages